# Architecture Rules

## Responsibilities

- Enforce Clean Architecture with clear layer boundaries
- Organize code feature-first, not by technical type alone
- Keep business logic independent of frameworks (Next.js, Prisma, UI)
- Define dependency direction: UI → Application → Domain ← Infrastructure

## Layer Model

```
Presentation  →  app/, components/, features/*/ui/
Application   →  features/*/actions/, features/*/hooks/, server/
Domain        →  features/*/types/, features/*/schemas/, shared/domain/
Infrastructure → repositories/, services/, prisma/, lib/
```

## Best Practices

- **Feature-first**: Group by domain (`features/cases/`, `features/clients/`)
- **Repository Pattern**: All DB access through repositories in `repositories/`
- **Dependency Injection**: Pass dependencies via constructor/factory, not global singletons
- **Server Components by default**: Client Components only when interactivity required
- **Server Actions** for mutations; Route Handlers only for webhooks/external APIs
- **Single Responsibility**: One reason to change per module
- **DRY**: Extract shared logic to `shared/` or `lib/`
- **KISS**: Prefer simple solutions over premature abstraction

## Coding Standards

- No business logic in React components — use hooks, services, or actions
- No direct Prisma calls from components or Server Actions — use repositories
- Cross-feature imports only through public API (`features/cases/index.ts`)
- Shared types in `types/` or feature-local `types.ts`
- Validate all external input with Zod at boundaries

## Folder Structure

```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router (routes, layouts, loading, error)
├── features/               # Feature modules (cases, clients, billing, etc.)
│   └── [feature]/
│       ├── ui/             # Feature-specific components
│       ├── actions/        # Server Actions
│       ├── hooks/          # React Query hooks
│       ├── schemas/        # Zod schemas
│       ├── types/          # Feature types
│       └── index.ts        # Public API barrel
├── components/             # Shared UI (layout, navigation, data-display)
├── shared/                 # Cross-cutting domain utilities
├── hooks/                  # Global reusable hooks
├── lib/                    # Framework config, utils, constants
├── server/                 # Server-only utilities, auth, middleware helpers
├── prisma/                 # Schema, migrations, seed
├── types/                  # Global TypeScript types
├── providers/              # React context providers
├── services/               # External integrations (email, storage, AI)
├── repositories/           # Data access layer
├── actions/                # Global server actions (auth, settings)
└── utils/                  # Pure utility functions
```

## Naming Convention

| Artifact | Convention | Example |
|----------|------------|---------|
| Feature folder | kebab-case, singular | `features/cases/` |
| Component | PascalCase | `CaseStatusBadge.tsx` |
| Hook | camelCase, `use` prefix | `useCases.ts` |
| Repository | PascalCase + Repository | `CaseRepository.ts` |
| Service | PascalCase + Service | `InvoiceService.ts` |
| Server Action | camelCase verb | `createCase.ts` |
| Type/Interface | PascalCase | `CaseWithClient` |
| Constant | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `MAX_FILE_SIZE` |

## Performance Rules

- Colocate data fetching with Server Components where possible
- Use React Query for client-side cache with stale-while-revalidate
- Paginate all list endpoints (default: 25 items)
- Lazy-load heavy feature modules and charts
- Avoid waterfall fetches — parallelize with `Promise.all`

## Security Rules

- Authenticate at middleware level; authorize at action/repository level
- Never expose internal IDs in URLs without access checks
- Audit log all destructive operations
- Sanitize all user-generated content before render

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — Repository abstracts Prisma
// repositories/case.repository.ts
export class CaseRepository {
  constructor(private db: PrismaClient) {}
  async findById(id: string, orgId: string) {
    return this.db.case.findFirst({ where: { id, organizationId: orgId } });
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD — Server Action delegates to service
// features/cases/actions/create-case.ts
export async function createCase(input: CreateCaseInput) {
  const session = await requireAuth();
  const parsed = createCaseSchema.parse(input);
  return caseService.create(parsed, session.userId);
}

// ❌ BAD — Prisma in component
const cases = await prisma.case.findMany(); // inside a .tsx file
```

## Things to Avoid

- God components (>300 lines)
- Circular dependencies between features
- Importing from `@/features/x/internal/...` — use public barrel only
- Mixing client and server code in same file
- Global mutable state outside React Query / URL state
- Anemic domain — put validation rules in schemas/services, not scattered in UI

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Code lives in the correct layer (UI vs application vs infrastructure)
- [ ] Feature has a public `index.ts` if consumed externally
- [ ] No direct DB access outside repositories
- [ ] Input validated with Zod at entry points
- [ ] Server/Client boundary respected (`"use client"` only when needed)
- [ ] No duplicate logic — checked `shared/` and existing features first
- [ ] Types exported and reused, not duplicated
